---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About · demo-web hub">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>About this project</h1>
    <p>I wanted to see which tools really work for publishing interactive learning content on GitHub Pages, so I built a small demo with each one and connected them here. Every site publishes a small <code>site.json</code>. At build time the hub fetches them and renders the cards. Each site's deploy workflow can trigger a hub rebuild through a <code>repository_dispatch</code> event.</p>
  </section>
  <section style="padding-bottom:56px">
    <h2>Add a new site</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Create the repo with its own framework, set its base path to <code>/&lt;repo&gt;/</code>.</li>
      <li>Publish <code>site.json</code>, <code>thumbnail.svg</code> and the hover-preview clips (<code>preview.webm</code>, <code>preview.mp4</code>) at the root of its built output.</li>
      <li>Add an entry to <code>src/data/sites.json</code> here.</li>
      <li>Optionally add the dispatch step so this hub rebuilds when the site deploys.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</Base>
